            <div xml:id="d663">

                <pb facs="0687" n="678" sameAs="frus:frus1938v05/pg678"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.52/3031</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Daniels</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 7155</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-08-03">August 3, 1938</date>.<lb/>[Received August
                        5.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to enclose herewith a
                    translation, subject to revision, of the Mexican reply to the American note on
                    agrarian compensation. <pb facs="0688" n="679" xml:id="pg679"/> This note was
                    handed to me this morning at 9 o’clock by General Hay and, due to the shortage
                    of time a copy of the Spanish text is not enclosed herewith but will be
                    forwarded by tomorrow’s air mail. For the same reason, I have not had time to
                    study the note and I am, therefore, making no comment.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Josephus Daniels</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d663-a1.xml" xpointer="d663-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
